# Physical-Effect Requests

[![Run in Livebook](https://livebook.dev/badge/v1/blue.svg)](https://livebook.dev/run?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Frefpath%2Fsigil_guard%2Fblob%2Fmain%2Fnotebooks%2Fphysical-effect-requests.livemd)

A tool call that moves an actuator needs more than an allow decision. The
host carries a binding record in the request metadata, the gateway digests it
into the decision, and `SigilGuard.EffectAuthority` checks the record against
current facts before the host releases the command. The cells use a fixed
clock and no hardware.

## Setup

```elixir
repo_root = Path.expand("..", __DIR__)
local_checkout? = File.regular?(Path.join(repo_root, "mix.exs"))

{sigil_guard_dep, install_opts} =
  if local_checkout? do
    {
      {:sigil_guard, path: repo_root, env: :prod},
      [
        config_path: Path.join(repo_root, "config/config.exs"),
        lockfile: Path.join(repo_root, "mix.lock")
      ]
    }
  else
    {{:sigil_guard, "~> 1.0"}, []}
  end

Mix.install([sigil_guard_dep], install_opts)
```

## Carry A Binding Record

The host puts the binding record under `_meta` of the tool call. With
`effect_binding: :required`, `ToolGateway.guard_request/3` refuses a request
without one and records the record's digest, `EffectAuthority.binding_digest/1`,
in the decision.

```elixir
alias SigilGuard.{EffectAuthority, ToolGateway}

program_sha256 = Base.encode16(:crypto.hash(:sha256, "pick-and-place v7"), case: :lower)

effect_record = %{
  "binding_format" => "sigil_guard_effect_binding/v1",
  "operation_id" => "op-0001",
  "target" => %{"id" => "urn:example:cell-a:arm-1", "environment" => "physical"},
  "artifacts" => [%{"name" => "program", "sha256" => program_sha256}],
  "frame_revision" => "cal-r3",
  "policy_epoch" => "example-bundle:42",
  "not_before" => "2026-11-19T12:00:00.000Z",
  "not_after" => "2026-11-19T12:05:00.000Z"
}

move_request = %{
  "jsonrpc" => "2.0",
  "id" => "move-1",
  "method" => "tools/call",
  "params" => %{
    "name" => "cell.move",
    "arguments" => %{"x_mm" => 250, "y_mm" => 100, "speed_mm_s" => 120},
    "_meta" => %{"dev.sigilguard/effect" => effect_record}
  }
}

cell_context = [
  phase: :tool_request,
  origin: :model,
  sink: :tool,
  actor: "spiffe://example.test/agent/planner",
  trust_level: :high,
  tool: "cell.move",
  action: "cell.move"
]

effect_decision = ToolGateway.guard_request(move_request, cell_context, effect_binding: :required)

without_record =
  move_request
  |> update_in(["params"], &Map.delete(&1, "_meta"))
  |> ToolGateway.guard_request(cell_context, effect_binding: :required)

:allowed = effect_decision.verdict
:effect_binding_required = without_record.audit_metadata.deny_reason
{:ok, binding_digest} = EffectAuthority.binding_digest(effect_record)
^binding_digest = effect_decision.audit_metadata.effect_binding_digest
64 = byte_size(effect_decision.audit_metadata.effect_operation_key)

%{
  bound: effect_decision.verdict,
  without_record: without_record.audit_metadata.deny_reason,
  ledger_key: effect_decision.audit_metadata.effect_operation_key,
  ledger_digests:
    Map.take(effect_decision.audit_metadata, [:action_digest, :payload_digest, :context_digest])
}
```

## Admit Against Current Facts

An allowed request is not yet a command. `EffectAuthority.admit/5` compares
the binding record with facts the host observes now and names the first fact
that does not hold.

```elixir
dispatch_time = ~U[2026-11-19 12:01:00.000Z]

current_facts = %{
  principal: "spiffe://example.test/agent/planner",
  target: %{id: "urn:example:cell-a:arm-1", environment: :physical},
  artifacts: [%{name: "program", sha256: program_sha256}],
  frame_revision: "cal-r3",
  policy_epoch: "example-bundle:42",
  observed_at: DateTime.add(dispatch_time, -100, :millisecond),
  now: dispatch_time
}

admit = fn facts ->
  EffectAuthority.admit(effect_decision, move_request, cell_context, facts, max_fact_age_ms: 500)
end

:ok = admit.(current_facts)

refusals = %{
  simulated_target: admit.(put_in(current_facts, [:target, :environment], :simulated)),
  recalibrated_frame: admit.(%{current_facts | frame_revision: "cal-r4"}),
  new_policy_epoch: admit.(%{current_facts | policy_epoch: "example-bundle:43"}),
  stale_facts: admit.(%{current_facts | observed_at: DateTime.add(dispatch_time, -5, :second)}),
  after_deadline:
    admit.(%{
      current_facts
      | now: ~U[2026-11-19 12:06:00.000Z],
        observed_at: ~U[2026-11-19 12:05:59.900Z]
    })
}

%{
  simulated_target: {:error, :target_environment_mismatch},
  recalibrated_frame: {:error, :frame_revision_mismatch},
  new_policy_epoch: {:error, :policy_epoch_mismatch},
  stale_facts: {:error, :stale_current_facts},
  after_deadline: {:error, :effect_deadline_passed}
} = refusals

refusals
```

## A Signed Report Is A Claim

A device report says what it did; it does not prove it.
`EffectAuthority.classify_outcome/1` sorts the report and `audit_fields/1`
gives the values to record.

```elixir
report = %{
  authentication: :verified,
  claimed: :success,
  issuer: "urn:example:cell-a:gateway",
  required_observations: 1
}

{:ok, claimed_only} = EffectAuthority.classify_outcome(Map.put(report, :observations, []))

{:ok, observed} =
  EffectAuthority.classify_outcome(
    Map.put(report, :observations, [
      %{source: "urn:example:cell-a:camera-1", result: :confirms}
    ])
  )

audit_fields = fn outcome ->
  {:ok, fields} =
    EffectAuthority.audit_fields(%{
      state: :finished,
      binding_digest: binding_digest,
      operation_key: effect_decision.audit_metadata.effect_operation_key,
      outcome: outcome
    })

  fields
end

:undetermined = claimed_only.acceptance
:accepted = observed.acceptance
nil = audit_fields.(claimed_only).result_info.success
true = audit_fields.(observed).result_info.success

%{
  signed_claim_alone: claimed_only.acceptance,
  with_an_observation: observed.acceptance,
  audit_result: audit_fields.(observed).result
}
```

